DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The ppaamm__ppuutteennvv() function sets an environment variable.  Its semantics
     are similar to those of putenv(3), but it modifies the PAM context's en‐
     vironment list instead of the application's.

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEESS
     The ppaamm__ppuutteennvv() function returns one of the following values:

     [PAM_SUCCESS]       Success.

     [PAM_BUF_ERR]       Memory buffer error.

     [PAM_SYSTEM_ERR]    System error.

